# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.so
.Python
build/
dist/
*.egg-info/
*.egg

# Virtual Environment
.venv/
venv/

# IDE
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# PyTorch models (large binary files)
models/*.pt
models/*.pth
data/training/*.pt

# Training datasets (regeneratable)
data/training/*.npz
data/datasets/

# bench/results/ is deliberately TRACKED (since 2026-08-07). "Regenerable" was wrong:
# a results file is hours of games, one was already destroyed by a filename collision,
# and an untracked results dir means no commit's headline number can be verified from
# a clone. Timings are machine-specific; game outcomes and Elo estimates are not.
# Run logs are console transcripts; the JSON results beside them are what is tracked.
bench/results/logs/

# bench/suites/ is deliberately TRACKED. The strength comparison is only valid if both
# arms run on the identical frozen position set, so the suite must be shared and stable
# across commits and machines — rebuilding it silently invalidates every prior number.

# Only the SERVED model is tracked. Experimental exports are 18MB each and would
# accumulate in history forever — an unadopted one already slipped in via `git add -A`.
models/*.onnx
!models/dual_model_mcts_fp32.onnx
!models/dual_model_mcts_int8.onnx

# NOTE: both of those are deliberately TRACKED, not ignored. They are what the web server
# actually serves, and keeping them in the repo is what makes a clone-based deploy work —
# see bench/test_deploy.py. int8 (4.8MB) is what inference.py prefers; fp32 (18.4MB) is
# kept because it is BOTH the fallback and the model int8 is quantised from, so dropping
# it would make the quantisation unreproducible from a clone. Torch checkpoints (*.pt)
# stay ignored: they are training artifacts, and the .onnx is regenerated from them by
# export_onnx.py.
models/*.onnx.data

# Stockfish binary (too large for git)
stockfish/
stockfish.exe

# Jupyter
.ipynb_checkpoints/
*.ipynb

# Database files
*.db

# Training logs
data/training/*.txt

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Native kernel build artifacts (rebuild: python native/setup_native.py build_ext --inplace)
native/build/
native/*.pyd
native/*.so
